*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.pytest_cache/
*.forged.epub

# Staged Java runtime and EPUBCheck; recreated by packaging/build.py
packaging/_bundle/

# Private corpus of real books — other people's work, never committed.
# Only the metric signatures under tests/corpus/expected/ are tracked, and the
# run ledger beside them: it holds a version, a date and five counts per run —
# no titles, no authors, not a byte of anyone's book. Entry into alpha asks for
# the corpus to be green "across three consecutive releases", and that is a
# claim about this project. A claim whose evidence lives on two private disks
# is not one anybody else can check.
tests/corpus/*
!tests/corpus/expected/
!tests/corpus/runs.json

# The public corpora are generated and committed, so they are green by
# construction and a log of their runs is evidence for nothing. Recording them
# also drops a `runs.json` straight into `tests/`, beside the test modules,
# which is the same trap as the ledger landing among the signatures: a file in
# a directory that means something else.
tests/runs.json
tests/corpus_gutenberg/runs.json

# Skonsolidowany audyt i jego artefakty żyją w prywatnym repozytorium notatek.
# Wróciły tu raz przez `git add -A` po przepisaniu historii; to je zatrzymuje.
audit_consolidation/
